[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3896773889","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116246#issuecomment-3896773889","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116246","id":3896773889,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oRA0B","user":{"login":"Vukbo","id":11051231,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDUxMjMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11051231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo","html_url":"https://github.com/Vukbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T11:51:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T11:51:22Z","body":"I did some investigation inside godot's source code. \nIt seems that upper and lower limits are inverted when using JoltPhysics. \nSwitching them lower and upper limits inside jolt_generic_6dof_joint_3d.cpp seems to fix the mismatch.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3896773889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897445581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116246#issuecomment-3897445581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116246","id":3897445581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oTkzN","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T14:11:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T14:11:21Z","body":"You can fix this by switching the world node to be Node B:\n\n<img width=\"2104\" height=\"1279\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e79c8c27-e079-4134-8cac-9e894ee680c5\" />\n\nJolt by default uses Node A as the static world and Node B for the dynamic body. \n\nIf you look at the gizmo:\n\n<img width=\"1310\" height=\"778\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae42f554-301a-414a-ad4d-cb550ecde7e0\" />\n\nyou see that while you have configured the lower limit to -2 and the upper limit to 1, the actual range of motion you're getting is -1 to 2 (because everything is inverted if the dynamic body is Node A). For angular limits the inversion and resulting behavior is far worse: the joint limits rotate with the dynamic body instead of being attached to the world. I personally cannot wrap my mind around that behavior. This is why we chose to make Node A the static world by default.\n\nI wasn't aware of the gizmo visualization, but I think we need to fix the gizmo visualization instead of changing the World Node default in Jolt (also for rotation).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897445581/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897643895","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116246#issuecomment-3897643895","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116246","id":3897643895,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oUVN3","user":{"login":"Vukbo","id":11051231,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDUxMjMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11051231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo","html_url":"https://github.com/Vukbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T14:53:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T14:53:52Z","body":"I just tried the suggested setting from inside the editor settings. \nThere is still a mismatch between the drawn gizmos and the runtime behaviour. \n\nTo me it seems like the joint3D doesn't handle the transforms of the attached node properly. \nAs this issue only arises when joints and attached bodies global_position are not the same. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897643895/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897701980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116246#issuecomment-3897701980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116246","id":3897701980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oUjZc","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T15:05:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T15:05:50Z","body":"I don't see what you mean. Please attach a video / new MRP if you need to make any other changes beside setting the default World Node.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897701980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897735033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116246#issuecomment-3897735033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116246","id":3897735033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oUrd5","user":{"login":"Vukbo","id":11051231,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDUxMjMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11051231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo","html_url":"https://github.com/Vukbo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vukbo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T15:11:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T15:12:54Z","body":"<video controls src=\"https://youtu.be/WkV0Kb9wldU\"></video>   \nhttps://youtu.be/WkV0Kb9wldU\n\nHere is the video.\n1. showing that when global positions are aligned -> works as intended\n2. showing that when global positons are not aligned -> doesn't work as intended, as orange capsule doesn't move inside red and blue planes.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3897735033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3898404546","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116246#issuecomment-3898404546","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116246","id":3898404546,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7oXO7C","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-13T17:28:36Z","updated_at":"2026-02-13T19:02:24Z","body":"> * showing that when global positions are aligned -> works as intended\n> * showing that when global positons are not aligned -> doesn't work as intended, as orange capsule doesn't move inside red and blue planes.\n\nJoints only limit the relative transformations from the bodies' \"local frames\" (Unity calls these \"anchors\" I believe), and the built-in joint nodes will always set that to be whatever the transforms of the bodies are at the time the joint enters the scene tree (or when changing `node_a`/`node_b`), so what you're seeing is the expected behavior.\n\nTo achieve what you likely expect you'd need to be able to set/override the local frames for the bodies, which the built-in joint nodes don't currently allow.\n\nThere is a long-standing (somewhat vague) proposal to add this (godotengine/godot-proposals#313) as well as a pending pull request to at least add this to Generic6DOFJoint3D (#109886), which I have not really looked at, so can't vouch for.\n\nNote that the underlying `PhysicsServer3D` API does let you pass in these local frames, so it's technically possible to do this already if you're willing to create your own joint nodes: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_physicsserver3d.html#class-physicsserver3d-method-joint-make-generic-6dof","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3898404546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]